  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In standard Young&#39;s double-slit experiment, visible light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>350</mn><mo>nm</mo><mtext>,&#160;</mtext><mn>750</mn><mo>nm</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is used in both the slits. Distance between the slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>, and the distance of the screen from the slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. A thin glass slab&nbsp;<math><mrow><mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>1.5</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mtext>m</mtext></math>&nbsp;is placed in front of slit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Which among the following wavelengths is missing at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P,</mi></math>&nbsp;which is directly in front of slit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>?(Neglect dispersion of light)<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0068292.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 145px;\" /></p>\r",
